ses in  history including Lord of the Rings The  Hobbit and The Matrix franchises so it  makes perfect sense that an actor of his  caliber would also find a place in the  Marvel Cinematic Universe which he  quickly did when he played the villain  Red Skull and Captain America the First  Avenger unfortunately while he was glad  to have it go he didn't exactly enjoy  the experience we've been told Collider  it's not something I would want to do  again I think I've done my - with that  sort of film it was good to do it and  try it out but to be honest it's not the  sort of film I seek out and really am  excited by we being added that he signed  a multi picture deal and said Marvel  could have forced him to reprise the  role but also pointed out that it would  have been pretty silly to force a  performer to show up for a project they  don't want to be in  Mickey Rourke was an absolute scene  stealer is Yvonne Banco an Iron Man -  Rourke brought an underlying empathy and  humanity to the role that makes his  performance incredibly compelling but he  told Screen Rant that the way Vaughn  code was written was far too  one-dimensional for his taste he  explained the bad guy doesn't always  have to be one-dimensional you know the  performance I tried to bring to Van Co  ends up on the floor that could cause  you not to care as much not to want to  put that effort in when you try to make  it an intelligent bad guy this character  was hard because he was written as pure  evil unlike many of his colleagues who  loved being a part of the Marvel  Cinematic Universe idris elba has told  The Telegraph that plain Heimdall in the  MCU movies quickly became a chore for  him after spending eight months in South  Africa making  Nelson Mandela biopic Mandela Elva added  that coming back to shoot scenes for  Thor the dark world was torture  explaining I was actually falling down  from a spaceship so they had to put me  on a harness in this green screen studio  and in between takes I was s